PART 5 — HOSTINGER DEPLOYMENT GUIDE
==================================================

Create:

/release/HOSTINGER_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md

The guide must include step-by-step instructions for Hostinger.

Include two paths:

----------------------------------
PATH A — Hostinger Node.js App Deployment
----------------------------------

Use this if Hostinger plan supports Node.js Apps.

Steps should explain:
1. Prepare final zip or GitHub repository.
2. Open Hostinger hPanel.
3. Go to Websites.
4. Choose the target website/domain.
5. Open Dashboard.
6. Choose Node.js Apps / Web Apps if available.
7. Create or import Node.js app.
8. Upload project or connect GitHub repository.
9. Set install command:
   npm ci
10. Set build command:
   npm run build
11. Set start command:
   npm run start
   or the correct production start command for this project.
12. Set Node version recommended by the project.
13. Add environment variables.
14. Configure domain.
15. Run migrations.
16. Run seed only if demo data is needed.
17. Test login.
18. Test checkout.
19. Test protected dashboards.
20. Test file uploads.
21. Test email/payment placeholders.

Also include:
- What to do if build fails.
- What logs to check.
- What env variables are usually missing.
- How to redeploy after changes.

----------------------------------
PATH B — File Manager / public_html Upload
----------------------------------

Use this only if the project is static or if a static export was intentionally created.

Steps:
1. Build static export if supported.
2. Create final static output folder.
3. Open Hostinger hPanel.
4. Go to Websites → Dashboard.
5. Open File Manager.
6. Open public_html.
7. Upload the static files/zip.
8. Extract files inside public_html.
9. Make sure index.html exists inside public_html.
10. Test the domain.

Warn clearly:
This method is not enough for a full app with backend/API/auth/database unless the backend is hosted somewhere else.

----------------------------------
PATH C — VPS Deployment
----------------------------------

Use this if Hostinger plan does not support Node.js Apps or if the project needs full server control.

Include high-level steps:
1. Create VPS.
